      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AKIRA SAN (3) put a real margin on them to shed her maiden tag over the mile here last time as a well-supported favourite, and her earlier eye-catching third here gives the form more depth. Gets weight relief and profiles to relish the rise in trip. Can win again. CHANCE DE LUNE (1) is the main danger on his comfortable Ipswich Mdn win two starts back, and he now comes back from a CL3 run that was too sharp late for him. READY TO DRINK (4) was second at the Gold Coast after having trouble getting clear near the 400m, and that gives her enough substance for a minor hope if she repeats it. BLOOD RED (5) continues to leave himself with too much to do but gets the chance to be closer in the small field. Similar story for MISSILE AWAY (6).",
